WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.382
The final coding exercise combines preservation, cardinality, and aggregation.

00:00:05.382 --> 00:00:11.637
The final result must contain one row per department, including departments with zero activity.

00:00:11.637 --> 00:00:17.027
That tells you to start from departments because departments is the population to preserve.

00:00:17.027 --> 00:00:22.207
LEFT JOIN admissions by department and LEFT JOIN medical staff by department.

00:00:22.207 --> 00:00:29.467
Because one department can have several admissions and several staff members, the combined rows can multiply.

00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:33.982
If you count every joined row directly, the measures can be inflated.

00:00:33.982 --> 00:00:39.892
Count distinct admission IDs for admission count and distinct staff IDs for staff count.

00:00:39.892 --> 00:00:44.612
Then GROUP BY department so the final grain is one row per department.

00:00:44.612 --> 00:00:48.332
After Run and Check, find the department with no activity.

00:00:48.332 --> 00:00:50.997
It should still appear with zero counts.

00:00:50.997 --> 00:00:56.807
Then inspect a busy department and make sure the values represent real admissions and real staff rather than

00:00:56.807 --> 00:00:59.478
multiplied join combinations.
